    {
      "id": "table-9",
      "line": 254,
      "heading_context": "## Common Confusion Points",
      "headers": [
        "Confusion",
        "Correction"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "\"LLVM is the Rust compiler.\"",
          "LLVM is the default backend. rustc owns Rust semantics and the middle end."
        ],
        [
          "\"LLVM IR is a stable Rust IR.\"",
          "It is a version-sensitive backend handoff/debug artifact."
        ],
        [
          "\"Cranelift changes the language.\"",
          "It changes code generation trade-offs after type checking and MIR."
        ],
        [
          "\"The GCC backend is gccrs.\"",
          "No. `rustc_codegen_gcc` is a rustc backend; gccrs is a separate GCC front end."
        ],
        [
          "\"LTO is just a linker flag.\"",
          "It coordinates rustc CGUs, LLVM summaries/bitcode, and linker behavior."
        ],
        [
          "\"BOLT is another `-C` backend option.\"",
          "BOLT is post-link binary optimization, used notably in rustc's own build pipeline."
        ],
        [
          "\"`target-cpu=native` is portable.\"",
          "It bakes in host CPU assumptions; use only when deployment hardware matches."
        ]
      ]
    },
